<title>VENEZUELA: Trinidad to award exploration licenses in June.</title>
<headline>Trinidad to award exploration licenses in June.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>At least 10 international petroleum companies have shown interest in Trinidad and Tobago's exploration licensing round which will be awarded in early June, an Trinidad government official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Exxon, Shell, Amoco, Conoco, British Gas, Texaco, Agip, ARCO, Union Texas and Petrobras were all participating in the bidding process to explore in offshore areas in over 750 metres of water, he added.</p>
<p>Trinidad currently produces about 130,000 barrels per day of oil and 700 million cubic feet per day of gas in association with nine foreign oil companies.</p>
<p>It has also begun construction of a $1 billion liquefied Natural Gas (LNG) plant due to come on stream in May 1999.</p>
<p>((-- Tom Ashby, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2611))</p>
